{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-158572" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $z=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x-2y+4)$ at the point $(-4,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158572" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To evaluate our multivariable function at the point $(-4,1),$ we substitute $x=-4$ and $y=1$ into the function expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\,{|}_{(-4,1)} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x-2y+4)\\,{|}_{(-4,1)} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3(-4)-2(1)+4) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-12-2+4) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-10),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is undefined." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158572" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2bebfa6c04569da3184fc3fe81406eb49baf53849082f46c98ed9f1f03b34b4c"} {"question" "q-158572" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158572" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡10"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡5"] ["text" "Undefined"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158572" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "Undefined"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158591" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The function $f(x,y)$ is defined as \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\sqrt[3]{xy+7}.\n$$\n\nEvaluate this function at the point $(-4,-5).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158591" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To evaluate our multivariable function at the point $(-4,-5),$ we substitute $x=-4$ and $y=-5$ into the function expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-4,-5) & =\\sqrt[3]{xy+7}\\,{|}_{(-4,-5)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{(-4)(-5)+7} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{20+7} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{27} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158591" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2bebfa6c04569da3184fc3fe81406eb49baf53849082f46c98ed9f1f03b34b4c"} {"question" "q-158591" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158591" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "2\\sqrt[3]{3}"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\sqrt[3]{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158591" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $z=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-1$ at the point $(3,{e}^{2}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To evaluate our multivariable function at the point $(3,{e}^{2}),$ we substitute $x=3$ and $y={e}^{2}$ into the function expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\,{|}_{(3,{e}^{2})} & =(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-1){|}_{(3,{e}^{2})} \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})-1 \\\\  & =3(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡e)-1 \\\\  & =3(2)-1 \\\\  & =6-1 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2bebfa6c04569da3184fc3fe81406eb49baf53849082f46c98ed9f1f03b34b4c"} {"question" "q-158574" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158574" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158574" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158592" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The function $f(x,y)$ is defined as \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.\n$$\n\nEvaluate this function at the point $(-6,-\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158592" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To evaluate our multivariable function at the point $(-6,-\\frac{\\pi }{4}),$ we substitute $x=-6$ and $y=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ into the function expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-6,-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,{|}_{(-6,-\\pi /4)} \\\\  & =-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-6(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158592" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2bebfa6c04569da3184fc3fe81406eb49baf53849082f46c98ed9f1f03b34b4c"} {"question" "q-158592" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158592" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "3\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158592" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158588" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The function $f(x,y)$ is defined as \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=3{y}^{3}-x+2.\n$$\n\nEvaluate this function at the point $(5,-1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158588" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To evaluate our multivariable function at the point $(5,-1),$ we substitute $x=5$ and $y=-1$ into the function expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(5,-1) & =(3{y}^{3}-x+2){|}_{(5,-1)} \\\\  & =3(-1)^{3}-5+2 \\\\  & =-3-5+2 \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158588" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2bebfa6c04569da3184fc3fe81406eb49baf53849082f46c98ed9f1f03b34b4c"} {"question" "q-158588" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158588" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "-7"] ["math" "10"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158588" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the domain of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{1}{2x+y}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\n2x+y\\ne 0\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,2x+y\\ne 0}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2bebfa6c04569da3184fc3fe81406eb49baf53849082f46c98ed9f1f03b34b4c"} {"question" "q-158553" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158553" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,2x+y<1}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,2x+y>0}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,2x+y\\ne -1}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,2x+y\\ne 0}"] ["text" "The domain is the entire $xy-$plane"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158553" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,2x+y\\ne 0}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158558" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the domain of the function $z=\\frac{\\sqrt{x-1}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158558" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero, and\n\n- the expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-1\\ge 0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-1\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}x\\ge 1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x\\ge 1,\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158558" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2bebfa6c04569da3184fc3fe81406eb49baf53849082f46c98ed9f1f03b34b4c"} {"question" "q-158558" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158558" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x<1,\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 0}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x=1,\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 1}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x\\ge 1,\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 0}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x\\ge 1,\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 1}"] ["text" "The domain is the entire $xy-$plane"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158558" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x\\ge 1,\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 1}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the domain of the function $z=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero, and\n\n- the expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}>0\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2bebfa6c04569da3184fc3fe81406eb49baf53849082f46c98ed9f1f03b34b4c"} {"question" "q-158179" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivari