isfy the following inequalities: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}>0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}>0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\ne 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}>0,\\,{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\ne 1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2bebfa6c04569da3184fc3fe81406eb49baf53849082f46c98ed9f1f03b34b4c"} {"question" "q-158577" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158577" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}>0,\\,{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\ne 1}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}>0}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}>1}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\ne 0,1}"] ["text" "The domain is the entire $xy$-plane"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158577" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}>0,\\,{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\ne 1}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158181" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the domain of the function  $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x-y).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158181" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The argument of the arccosine has values between $-1$ and $1.$\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\n-1\\le x-y\\le 1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-1\\le x-y\\le 1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158181" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2bebfa6c04569da3184fc3fe81406eb49baf53849082f46c98ed9f1f03b34b4c"} {"question" "q-158181" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158181" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-1\\le x-y\\le 1,\\,x>0}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-1\\le x-y\\le 1}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le x-y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0\\le x-y\\le \\pi }"] ["text" "The domain is the entire $xy$-plane"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158181" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-1\\le x-y\\le 1}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158180" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the domain of the function $z=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)}{y}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158180" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive, and\n\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+y>0 \\\\ y\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x+y>0,\\,y\\ne 0}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158180" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2bebfa6c04569da3184fc3fe81406eb49baf53849082f46c98ed9f1f03b34b4c"} {"question" "q-158180" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158180" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x+y>0,\\,y>0}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x+y>0,\\,y\\ne 0}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x+y>0}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x+y\\ge 0}"] ["text" "The domain is the entire $xy$-plane"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158180" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x+y>0,\\,y\\ne 0}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the domain of the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that\n\n- ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ is defined for all $x$ and $y,$ and\n\n- $\\operatorname{sin}⁡g(x,y)$ is defined if $g(x,y)$ is defined.\n\nAs a result, $\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})$ is defined for all values of $x$ and $y.$ This means that the domain of $f$ is the entire $xy$-plane." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2bebfa6c04569da3184fc3fe81406eb49baf53849082f46c98ed9f1f03b34b4c"} {"question" "q-158573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<2\\pi }"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=0}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>0}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 0}"] ["text" "The domain is the entire $xy$-plane"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "The domain is the entire $xy$-plane"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158198" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following shaded regions corresponds to the domain of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158198" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\ge 0\\,⟹\\,{y}^{2}\\le {x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,-|x|\\le y\\le |x|\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-|x|\\le y\\le |x|}.\n$$\n\nSince the inequality involves the $\\le $ sign, the curves are part of the domain. Therefore, we draw the solid curves $y=-|x|$ and $y=|x|,$ and shade the area *below* the curve $y=|x|,$ and *above* the curve $y=-|x|.$\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/95f187d2857973e4fea83eedf47bd54c153ce2a77f278cfb992b222de2d91ab8.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/qu