ltivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158202" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/89076b709a935f384acab2609f2d046123ceb3984c5ae60818f908525ad5e53d.png"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158195" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following shaded regions corresponds to the domain of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-1}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158195" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-1\\ge 0\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 1}.\n$$\n\nSince the inequality involves the $\\ge $ sign, the curve ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1$ is part of the domain. Therefore, we draw a solid curve ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1$ and shade the area *outside* the curve.\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/ba31bbc16c58860a4bc3c4d33ea1a61cb3d86d0e73d8aa6a67869b3e96a7fe32.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158195" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2bebfa6c04569da3184fc3fe81406eb49baf53849082f46c98ed9f1f03b34b4c"} {"question" "q-158195" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158195" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/1c1d7ca7d9fdcaa8baeded0408339b29130810c07fb90b27ebc0674f9bffa275.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/2ddf4edfd91b14835e7b14ca8cebf08b82b8585d9fd18972c8b065d6153a62f0.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/488ae413d28377a5dcd8887003e5389c082189867c0d3cdf0564d4a2f351ed56.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/7afd18ecf16e868bb65e43626144251a1387d3dbbac8ec552ab1f8544b35d6fe.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/b7cf0f04bb0ac9373b222edef23d2925ea40d06fafa33f03423220f99de7d95f.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158195" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/b7cf0f04bb0ac9373b222edef23d2925ea40d06fafa33f03423220f99de7d95f.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158205" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following shaded regions corresponds to the domain of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158205" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 0\\,⟹\\,(x,y)\\ne (0,0)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,(x.y)\\ne (0,0)}.\n$$\n\nSince the expression involves the $\\ne $ sign, the point $(0,0)$ is *not* part of the domain. Therefore, we exclude the point $(x,y)=(0,0)$ and shade the plane.\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/701c54bff1c431883f21cb980ac43f4f2f6beabb11817066a4e909d5a2663a25.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158205" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2bebfa6c04569da3184fc3fe81406eb49baf53849082f46c98ed9f1f03b34b4c"} {"question" "q-158205" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158205" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/402d90507403eabf4cd35cde83a45c9fa2d8080347e1debb0e2463be408b489b.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/4789f1e3a4fbe0c6f23980010a0222905cb46b4ef105b02e7fba0b59fc570eeb.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/65e29ff9fda5ad25fbbd68121d0c1a86e27a41de8890af31425208d7c38f2c2f.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/c30be01de07727a44fce390cfc2c56ddeed8071a7a7d64abec831a31aa2079fe.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/fefbca84defd52b9fecd3b13b37cb95a744b4ddedd5a570ad554b6a251cd6077.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158205" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/fefbca84defd52b9fecd3b13b37cb95a744b4ddedd5a570ad554b6a251cd6077.png"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158193" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following shaded regions corresponds to the domain of the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}-{y}^{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158193" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The function $f(x,y)$ is defined for all points $(x,y)$ on the plane, hence the domain is the entire $xy$-plane. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/402d90507403eabf4cd35cde83a45c9fa2d8080347e1debb0e2463be408b489b.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158193" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2bebfa6c04569da3184fc3fe81406eb49baf53849082f46c98ed9f1f03b34b4c"} {"question" "q-158193" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158193" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/09a061a81ca4b3201e9b97ad15354c14003e41d610c2892f5b6ba468761e83b7.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/338809ca0a3fe4d02c3523ec5e34a8d07a00b297d9f468740bbd1800d9675941.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/39360eae2b0e74a944c4e5c40e5677460c10b3259824fd400d20c5fd5ec9a23e.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/402d90507403eabf4cd35cde83a45c9fa2d8080347e1debb0e2463be408b489b.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/b8fe923f727ca57a8a2cfc756b93c0ed522bdd9edcc06c8097bead979c8e4b15.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "q-158193" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/402d90507403eabf4cd35cde83a45c9fa2d8080347e1debb0e2463be408b489b.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/state.json" "file_sha256" "57e34bca2cf6248dc15946bcf549089887650af38a2378f938f7cd8c0b8190fa"} {"question" "e-11025" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The function $f(x,y)$ is defined as \n\n$$\nf(x,y) = y^2 - \\log_3(x - 7).\n$$\n\nEvaluate this function at the point $(10,3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/example-11025.json" "file_sha256" "0823c6262f2b1f30e50451ec1d4284040ccfff8d28e80e74f65e69db7446acf3"} {"question" "e-11025" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To evaluate our multivariable function at the point $(10,3),$ we substitute $x = 10$ and $y = 3$ into the function expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(10,3) & =({y}^{2}-{log}_{3}⁡(x-7)){|}_{(10,3)} \\\\  & ={3}^{2}-{log}_{3}⁡(10-7) \\\\  & =9-{log}_{3}⁡(3) \\\\  & =9-1 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(10,3)=8.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/example-11025.json" "file_sha256" "0823c6262f2b1f30e50451ec1d4284040ccfff8d28e80e74f65e69db7446acf3"} {"question" "e-11021" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the domain of the function $z = \\dfrac {\\sqrt {y+1}}{x+y}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/example-11021.json" "file_sha256" "473983ff9943fa3ad0e4029aacd672ee3471cc1d9cce845ec63f4c9d9a40b7a3"} {"question" "e-11021" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero, and\n\n- the expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/6fa2a35bd31547c7ee3931d9c21defc69be918fb57c8ceb26ce9f19e1a77c816.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\big\\{ (x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,:\\, y \\geq -1, \\: y \\neq -x \\big\\}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/example-11021.json" "file_sha256" "473983ff9943fa3ad0e4029aacd672ee3471cc1d9cce845ec63f4c9d9a40b7a3"} {"question" "e-11029" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the domain of the function $z= \\dfrac{\\ln (2x+y)}{\\sqrt{x}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/example-11029.json" "file_sha256" "a73096bc89b853c810c23cab71ed990d75035dee5801e032bd89caf36e170ca9"} {"question" "e-11029" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive,\n\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero, and\n\n- the expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+y>0 \\\\ x>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\big\\{(x, y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,:\\, 2x+y >0, \\: x > 0 \\big\\}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/example-11029.json" "file_sha256" "a73096bc89b853c810c23cab71ed990d75035dee5801e032bd89caf36e170ca9"} {"question" "e-11022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Sketch the domain of $g(x,y)=\\dfrac{1}{\\ln(x+y)}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/example-11022.json" "file_sha256" "0aa5f4aca720dc4ef6d462cf54d3e070f4987b771440ac6357044bdc32e839ed"} {"question" "e-11022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive, and\n\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/b3e80f16cf1d83b9e6936a77fbd8c165a610bc5bff73b39521b03058e5b066b2.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\nD = \\left \\{ (x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\, : \\, y \\gt -x, \\, y \\neq 1-x \\right \\}.\n$$\n\nNow, we plot the corresponding domain. \n\n- Starting with $y> -x,$ we draw a dashed line $y=-x$ and shade the region *above* the line.\n\n- Then, we draw a dashed line $y=1-x$ through the shaded region.\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/assets/6aa1aaeadb177cf5a80bcb12a247725cb3396586e7516c3ba30b46b03a9d2612.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/example-11022.json" "file_sha256" "0aa5f4aca720dc4ef6d462cf54d3e070f4987b771440ac6357044bdc32e839ed"}] "usage" {"e-11022" [] "q-158195" [] "e-11021" [] "e-11029" [] "q-158182" [] "q-158180" [] "e-11025" [] "q-158181" []} "basis" 1529 "retractions" [[17592186124717 :question/problem "Find the domain of the function $f(x, y) = \\frac{xy}{x^{2} + y^{2}}$."] [17592186124716 :question/problem "Find the domain of the function $f(x, y) = \\arccos (x - y)$."] [17592186124715 :question/problem "Find the domain of the function $z = (\\ln (x + y))/(y)$."] [17592186124718 :question/problem "Which of the following shaded regions corresponds to the domain of the function $f(x, y) = \\sqrt{x^{2} + y^{2} - 1}$?"] [17592186124114 :question/problem "The function $f(x,y)$ is defined as\n$f(x,y) = y^2 - \\log_3(x - 7)$.\nEvaluate this function at the point $(10,3)$."] [17592186124114 :question/worked-solution "To evaluate our multivariable function at the point $(10,3)$, we substitute $x = 10$ and $y = 3$ into the function expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(10, 3) &= (y^{2} - \\log_{3} (x - 7)) \\mid _{(10, 3)} \\\\\n&= 3^{2} - \\log_{3} (10 - 7) \\\\\n&= 9 - \\log_{3} (3) \\\\\n&= 9 - 1 \\\\\n&= 8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nf(10,3)=8\n$$"] [17592186124112 :question/problem "Find the domain of the function $z = \\dfrac {\\sqrt {y+1}}{x+y}$."] [17592186124112 :question/worked-solution "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero, and\n- the expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n$$\n{y + 1 \\ge 0; x + y \\ne 0\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\big\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,:\\, y \\geq -1, \\: y \\neq -x \\big\\}\n$$"] [17592186124116 :question/problem "Find the domain of the function $z= \\dfrac{\\ln (2x+y)}{\\sqrt{x}}$."] [17592186124116 :question/worked-solution "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive,\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero, and\n- the expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n${2x + y > 0; x > 0$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\big\\{(x, y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,:\\, 2x+y >0, \\: x > 0 \\big\\}\n$$"] [17592186124113 :question/problem "Sketch the domain of $g(x,y)=\\dfrac{1}{\\ln(x+y)}$."] [17592186124113 :question/worked-solution "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive, and\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n$$\n{x + y > 0; \\ln (x + y) \\ne 0\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\nD = \\left \\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,: \\, y \\gt -x, \\, y \\neq 1-x \\right \\}\n$$\n\nNow, we plot the corresponding domain.\n\n- Starting with $y> -x$, we draw a dashed line $y=-x$ and shade the region *above* the line.\n- Then, we draw a dashed line $y=1-x$ through the shaded region.\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1899/Source/Images/bcd5261dc88387b9f76d0ff643039167.png)"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186121310 17592186121311 17592186121312 17592186121313 17592186121314 17592186121316 17592186121317 17592186121318 17592186121319 17592186121320 17592186121322 17592186121323 17592186121324 17592186121325 17592186121326 17592186121328 17592186121329 17592186121330 17592186121331 17592186121332] "immutable_fields" [[17592186121309 :answer-field/correct] [17592186121309 :answer-field/id] [17592186121309 :answer-field/key] [17592186121309 :answer-field/type] [17592186121315 :answer-field/correct] [17592186121315 :answer-field/id] [17592186121315 :answer-field/key] [17592186121315 :answer-field/type] [17592186121321 :answer-field/correct] [17592186121321 :answer-field/id] [17592186121321 :answer-field/key] [17592186121321 :answer-field/type] [17592186121327 :answer-field/correct] [17592186121327 :answer-field/id] [17592186121327 :answer-field/key] [17592186121327 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
